# Queues and cron

Queues (BullMQ)
- Definitions under app/server/queues/
  - backupQueue.ts
  - plaidSyncQueue.ts and plaidSyncBalanceQueue.ts
  - recalculateQueue.ts
- Use server/lib/queueManager.ts and server/clients/queuesClient.ts for consistent setup
- Admin UI via @bull-board/h3 is present as a dependency; SHOW_BULL_MQ_ADMIN controls visibility in prod manifests

## Plaid jobs (balance vs transactions)

- Transaction sync (`plaid-sync`) should call **inline** `/accounts/get` balance update after txn apply (`PlaidSyncService.syncBalancesForAccessToken`). Do not rely only on enqueuing balance jobs.
- Balance queue (`plaid-sync-balance`): by default skips registers with `plaidBalanceLastSyncAt` within the last **6 hours**.
- `addPlaidBalanceSyncJob({ force: true })`: delay 0 and a unique `jobId` (timestamp suffix) so manual/task syncs are not deduped or delayed.
- Hourly cron `plaid-balance.hourly.ts` enqueues one job per distinct access token for stale/null `plaidBalanceLastSyncAt`.
- See `.agent/logic/plaid.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/plaid-sync.mdc`.

Cron jobs (nuxt-cron)
- app/server/cron/* — scheduled tasks, e.g.:
  - backup.daily.ts
  - bill-reminders.hourly.ts
  - plaid.daily.ts, plaid-balance.hourly.ts
  - recalculate.hourly.ts
- Cron triggers should enqueue work onto queues; keep cron handlers lightweight and idempotent

Tasks endpoints
- app/server/api/tasks/* — http-invoked maintenance/debug triggers (seed, migrate, sync, test helpers)
- Gate dangerous tasks behind internal tokens or admin checks
- `sync-plaid-balance` uses `force: true`

Guidelines
- Prefer small jobs with retries and observability (IntegrationJobLog for external-facing work)
- Avoid long DB transactions in workers; batch work and checkpoint
- Ensure Redis availability is validated via clients/redisClient.ts
